{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation interface, separating sensor outcomes from motion commands. The specification encodes the safe exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, directed recovery (turns or, as last resort, full_rotate). Recovery states are one-shot and return to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and only one controllable is enabled per state to avoid oscillation.",
